"s:SH"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each call is entered with the vertex it adds to R, the clique being grown, and the contents of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"R, of P, the candidates that extend R, and of X, the vertices that extend it but were already"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tried. The outer calls take the vertices in "},{"code":"coreNumbers().degeneracyOrdering","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", each v with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"R = {v}, P its neighbors after it and X its neighbors before it (Eppstein, Löffler and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Strash). A call with P and X both empty reports R as a maximal clique. A call with candidates"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"chooses Tomita’s pivot, the member of P ∪ X with the most neighbors in P (ties to the least"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertex index), and then calls itself on each candidate not adjacent to the pivot, in index"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order, moving that candidate from P to X after the call. Every call ends with a backtrack."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Self-loops and parallel edges are ignored."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:7Cliques17BronKerboschEventO","modules":[{"name":"Cliques"}],"symbolKind":"enum","remoteSource":{"fileName":"BronKerboschEvents.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Cliques\/BronKerboschEvents.swift#L16"},"roleHeading":"Enumeration","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"BronKerboschEvent"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BronKerboschEvent","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"BronKerboschEvent"},"sc